{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KJvWdrrPb3LmSYsSNxfqhx","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_fm_rate.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets\nfm_totals = fact.aggregate(total_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population\nus_pop = ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\").select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fm_totals.join(us_pop, fm_totals.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(rate_per_100k=fm_totals.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"rate_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I now have:\n- Total farmers markets: 7,944\n- US population (2025): 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to calculate the rate per 100,000:\n(7944 / 341784857) * 100000\n\nLet me use xorq_select to calculate this metric to four decimal places. I'll create a build script that joins these values and computes the metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me calculate the rate per 100,000 residents. I'll create a build script that computes this metric:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01KJvWdrrPb3LmSYsSNxfqhx","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_fm_rate.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Read census data\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census\", storage_options=so)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets\nfm_totals = fact.aggregate(total_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US population\nus_pop = ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\").select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fm_totals.join(us_pop, fm_totals.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(rate_per_100k=fm_totals.total_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"rate_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic